SUMMARY:Gap Relief Auction
DESCRIPTION:Join an annual community celebration of generosity with food and a quilt and variety auction to support the relief\, development and peace work of Mennonite Central Committee. \nFriday\, August 7 \n\n4:00 – 7:00 p.m. Pork Supper (eat-in or take out)\n4:00 – 9:00 p.m. Food Court\n6:00 p.m. Auction Starts\n7:15 p.m. Singing & MCC Speaker\n\nSaturday\, August 8 \n\n6:00 a.m. Country breakfast (pancakes\, sausages and eggs)\n8:30 a.m.  Food Court Opens\n8:00 a.m. – 1:00 p.m. Silent Auction\n8:30 a.m. – 2:30 pm – Children’s Activities\n\nBounce House\nBarrel Train\nAuction (see block #3)\n\n\nBlock 1 Auction\n\n8:30 a.m. – Household items\n11:00 a.m. – Furniture\n12:00 p.m. – Special items\n1:00 p.m. – Quilts\n\n\nBlock 2 Auction\n\n9:00 a.m. – Tools and Farm Related Items\n\n\nBlock 3 Auction\n\n9:15 a.m. – Children’s Auction\n10:30 a.m. – Plants and Flowers\, Lawn Furniture & Outdoor items\, shrubbery\, outdoor lawn furniture\n1:00 p.m. – Larger Outdoor Items\n\nItems may include\n\nHunting Blind\nGreenhouse\nShed/Playhouse\nSwing Set\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBlock 4 (in Food Court)\n\n2:30 p.m. – Surplus food\n\n\n\n\nMud Sales are a unique Lancaster County tradition to raise funds for local volunteer fire companies. See our complete schedule of Lancaster County mud sales. \nPlease Note: Many of the Fire Companies holding mud sales can always use extra help on the days they receive items and the day of the event.  It takes a LOT of labor to put on a mud sale. \n 
URL:https://lancasterpa.com/events-calendar/gap-relief-auction-2/2026-08-07/
LOCATION:Solonco Fairgrounds\, 172 S. Lime Street\, Quarryville\, PA\, 17566\, United States
